<!-- Section 9: Twelve practical examples -->
<section id="sec-practical" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Real-Life Applications of Right Triangle Perimeter and Semiperimeter</h2>
  <p>Twelve worked situations carry the two formulas from the page into the workshop and the site. Each one names a simplified right-triangular object or model, works the perimeter and semiperimeter through the formulas, and states the practical reading of the result. These are simplified models: not every real window, roof, garden, awning, panel, or support structure forms an exact right triangle, and an irregular object must be divided into simpler shapes before the formulas apply. Material allowances may be needed, cutting waste is not included, curved boundaries require different calculations, structural strength cannot be determined from perimeter alone, and actual construction measurements should be verified before purchasing materials.</p>

  <h3>Example 1: Triangular Glass Window Frame</h3>
  <p>A right-triangular window has <span set:html={rich('[[a=3\\text{ m}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b=4\\text{ m}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[c=5\\text{ m}]]')} />. Perimeter: <span set:html={rich('[[P=3+4+5]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{P=12\\text{ m}}]]]')} />. Semiperimeter: <span set:html={rich('[[s=\\frac{12}{2}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{s=6\\text{ m}}]]]')} />. Twelve metres is the total length around the window&apos;s triangular outline: the frame stock to order before mitre and waste allowances.</p>

  <h3>Example 2: Roof Edge Trim</h3>
  <p>A triangular roof-end section has <span set:html={rich('[[a=6\\text{ ft}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b=8\\text{ ft}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[c=10\\text{ ft}]]')} />. Perimeter: <span set:html={rich('[[P=6+8+10]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{P=24\\text{ ft}}]]]')} />. Semiperimeter: <span set:html={rich('[[s=\\frac{24}{2}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{s=12\\text{ ft}}]]]')} />. The perimeter estimates the trim length around the triangular outline of the roof end.</p>

